  <dl>
    <dt>When to use NBD:</dt>
    <dd class="nbd-muted">Whole-disk imaging · cold backups · block recovery · not everyday file shares</dd>
  </dl>
  <blockquote class="inline_help">
    <strong>Use NBD</strong> for whole-disk or partition imaging to qcow2/raw (seekable, sparse-friendly),
    restorable cold copies before reinstall/migration, and block-level tools over a <em>private fast</em> link
    (Thunderbolt / 10G). Staging disk images next to high-performance peers is a good fit.<br><br>
    <strong>Use SMB or NFS</strong> when you only need files and folders.
    Prefer <strong>read-only</strong> and a private bind IP — never the public Internet.
    Docs:
    <a href="https://github.com/ibigsnet/NbdExport/blob/main/docs/when-to-use-nbd.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener">when to use ↗</a>
    ·
    <a href="https://github.com/ibigsnet/NbdExport/blob/main/DOCS.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener">full guide ↗</a>
  </blockquote>

